  - Pre-registered test: TypeSafe's Jev decision model trails Claude Opus 5.5 at 72.0% against 87.4% top-1 diagnosis  {}
  - Game-competition benchmark: Opus 5.5 with Claude Code took 6 gold medals against 1,920 archived human programs  {}
  - PDF line-break artifacts, not writing style, drive near-perfect AI-text detection on arXiv benchmarks  {}
  - Biosecurity benchmark: 67.6% of one-shot LLM mutation designs beat the average measured variant, and tools raise the risk  {}
  - Palantir CTO tells CBS that Bloomberg's reporting on the Minab strike is wrong and the likely cause is human error  {ai-weapons-targeting}
  - Palantir CTO says there has been no operational impact from the Pentagon dropping Anthropic, which is already replaced  {anthropic-pentagon-split}
  - Claude Code agents surveying 1.9 billion protein clusters surfaced a new family of jumbo-phage reverse transcriptases  {}
  - AI assistance raised pooled reader accuracy from 90.4% to 97.4% in neural autoantibody tissue reading  {}
  - Conformal-prediction model reproduced clinician MS disease-course labels at 98% sensitivity against 71% for the Lorscheider criteria  {}
  - Epileptologists correctly identified only 4 of 6 pairs of AI-fabricated and human-written seizure manuscripts  {}
  - Standardised-patient study: a ChatGPT 4o intake chatbot asked about 59.3% of critical elements on easy cases and 50.2% on difficult ones  {}
  - Epilepsy lesion detector loses specificity at 7T, falling to 39% from 76% on paired 3T scans  {}
  - UK says AI pilots found and fixed over 1,000 government vulnerabilities, and will explore covering AI loss of control in the Cyber Bill  {}
  - Microsoft's Brad Smith tells the BBC a washing machine faces more safety rules than AI and calls for an emergency brake  {agents-going-wrong}
  - Report: White House reverses course and restores UK AI Security Institute access to pre-release US models  {}
  - Broadcom and Intel chief executives say capital, not chips or power, may be the biggest constraint on AI  {compute-money}
  - SWI raises €800 million at a €6.1 billion valuation to convert FTX-linked bitcoin mining sites to AI  {compute-money}
  - IREN rose about 9% overnight after a report that Anthropic signed an undisclosed multiyear cloud deal with the miner  {compute-money}
  - IMF's Georgieva calls AI a slow-moving tsunami for jobs, with about 40% of jobs worldwide eventually affected  {}
