  - Marine Corps University opens a wargaming tournament pitting service members against an autonomous AI opponent  {}
  - Army adds a light variant to its autonomous Common Autonomous Multi-Domain Launcher programme  {}
  - JAMA study logs 271 million clinician queries to the OpenEvidence platform over 30 months  {}
  - SimBioSys says FDA cleared TumorSight Risk, an MRI-derived breast cancer recurrence risk tool, under 510(k)  {}
  - Insilico Medicine preprint reports AUROC 0.828 for predicting clinical trial efficacy from registration data  {}
  - Judge Stein stays the Times Publishing action in the OpenAI copyright MDL pending summary judgment  {}
  - UK Electoral Commission building deepfake flagging system; May pilot scanned 3 million posts and flagged 147  {}
  - OpenAI tells court more than 100 confidential files left with an employee who returned to Apple  {}
  - Investors discuss an Anthropic IPO valuation near $1.5 trillion, down from the roughly $2 trillion expected  {compute-money}
  - Taiwan plans US industrial parks for AI suppliers, starting with a Texas complex costing up to $4 billion  {}
  - Virginia senator files Senate Bill 843 for a three-year statewide data centre approval moratorium  {}
  - Accenture tells employees centrally funded Claude use is capped at $29 per person per month  {}
  - 404 Media details how ChatGPT ads target users by uploaded phone numbers, emails and prompt-based context hints  {}
  - Meta commercial terms effective 30 October let it crawl business accounts' own websites to train AI, lawyers say  {}
  - Simons Foundation, Anthropic and OpenAI commit $15 million to help mathematicians assess AI-assisted results  {mathematicians-vs-labs}
=== 2026-10-17 :: Anthropic measures itself and pitches Congress its own bill
  - DeepSeek releases V4.1-Flash-1017 under MIT, scoring 42.3 on Terminal-Bench 4.0 against 31.2 before  {}
  - Reflection AI publishes Beam's weights under Apache 2.0, 501B parameters with 23B active per token  {}
  - Anthropic says an internal research model traced NIST's ECDSA curve seeds to lrand48 and Unix timestamps  {}
  - Anthropic and Harvard report LLM-designed quantum circuits beating published designs on seven of eight tasks  {}
  - Epoch AI puts the best open-weight model's cyber capability 6-7 months behind the closed frontier  {}
  - Redwood Research pipeline turned 94 real agent transcripts into 35 attacks that evaded its monitors  {agents-going-wrong}
  - Benchmark finds LLM judges accept 88.6% to 94.1% of tampered deployments producing identical outputs  {}
