  - Police used an AI-generated image of a fictitious teenager to arrest a school worker, 404 Media reports  {}
  - Benchmark on real criminal cases: unsafe LLM compliance rises from 28.9% to 66.4% under corrective framing  {}
  - China's draft export catalogue adds 40 technologies, 23 of them AI, with 14 prohibited and 26 restricted  {china-distillation-export-controls}
  - Taiwan to add advanced AI chips and servers to its export control list, economics minister says  {china-distillation-export-controls}
  - Acting Navy secretary says the Theodore Roosevelt strike group deployed on 8 October with an unmanned surface vessel  {}
  - Germany tells Boeing it will not buy the MQ-28 Ghost Bat, pushing its drone wingman to the early 2030s  {}
  - Google Research agents reach a 42.1% aptamer hit rate at 98.5% specificity after three wet-lab cycles  {}
  - Multimodal AI beats InSilicoVA on cause of death by 8.5 to 15.9 points in 4,999 South African verbal autopsies  {}
  - Audit of 2,550 conversations finds chatbot persistence after refused crisis referrals ranging from 0.01 to 9.94  {}
  - NIST, NSA and CISA publish ten voluntary practices for incidents during super intelligence training  {agents-going-wrong}
  - Anthropic confirms it is circulating a draft federal AI bill with $1 billion and 50-casualty thresholds  {regulating-frontier-ai-us}
  - Unsealed filing says Microsoft told staff to keep the OpenAI crawler project codenamed Project Mango secret  {}
  - Apple updates App Review Guidelines to cover AI-generated nonconsensual intimate imagery and bait-and-switch apps  {}
  - Anthropic is offering Blackstone a yield of more than 10% on $9 billion of chip-lease debt, Reuters reports  {compute-money}
  - NVIDIA says RTX Spark laptops ship from six makers with up to 1 petaflop FP4 and 128GB unified memory  {}
  - Digital Realty plans a 1GW data centre campus on 476 acres in Kokomo, Indiana, built out by 2033  {}
  - UK rejects an AI Growth Zone bid for a 1.2GW data centre powered by Drax's biomass plant  {}
  - AI cloud Modal raises $750 million at a $15.75bn post-money valuation, five months after its Series C  {}
  - Anthropic says the junior share of its technical hires fell from 27% to 9% since early 2025  {}
  - Anthropic survey finds 91% of its staff and 39% of US adults expect a Nobel-level AI discovery by 2030  {}
  - Replit's chief executive says it has stopped working with Anthropic; insiders say the partnership stands  {}
  - Vercel reports open-weight models took 71.5% of gateway tokens in September as Anthropic's spend share fell  {}
=== 2026-10-18 :: Microsoft walks away from Britain's stalled AI data centre
  - Anthropic is consulting law firms on how its AI agents should negotiate on users' behalf  {}
  - OpenCode's maker says a breach tied to a large-scale distillation attack exposed provider API keys for 1.4% of Console users  {ai-enabled-hacking}
  - Taiwan's defence ministry awards ThinkTron a NT$46.55 million contract for AI analysis of satellite imagery  {}
  - Zen Technologies to buy 51.98% of Cogknit Semantics, which builds AI battlefield management systems, for ₹135.15 crore  {}
  - Meta deletes the word "train" from the web-crawling clause of commercial terms taking effect 30 October  {}
  - Anthropic's Jack Clark tells IMF meetings an internal model forecasts $44 trillion US output by 2030  {pacing-frontier-ai}
  - AP counts at least eight states suing OpenAI; Tech Policy Press maps 13 complaints filed on 13 and 14 October  {regulating-frontier-ai-us}
  - Microsoft cancels its anchor-tenant deal for 23,000 Nvidia chips at Nscale's Loughton site over a grid connection  {compute-money}
  - Oracle says a fuel-cell redesign cuts Project Jupiter greenhouse gases from 8.8 million to 5.7 million tons a year  {}
  - NVIDIA says RTX Spark laptops are now on sale from $2,399, with up to 1 petaflop of AI compute  {}
  - Replit's chief executive says OpenAI is now the default model behind Replit Agent, with Claude still selectable  {}
  - US cybersecurity job postings fell 26.4% while AI Security Engineer demand rose 268.3%, CyberSN report says  {}
=== 2026-10-19 :: Army Cyber Command wants agents that neutralise targets themselves
  - Anthropic commits 5% of its shares to a wholly owned public benefit fund, subject to stockholder approval  {compute-money}

